  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195000: Bounded chunked HTTP, endpoint canonicalization, and PostgreSQL query slice

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The Kotoba HTTP provider accepts a single case-insensitive `Transfer-Encoding:
chunked` field only when Content-Length is absent. It decodes chunks in place
under the caller's response cap. Chunk extensions, trailers, malformed hex,
truncation and CL/TE coexistence fail closed.

Transport hostnames use IDNA STD3 ASCII, lowercase and removal of one DNS root
dot. IPv4 and IPv6 literals use InetAddress canonical numeric form; IPv6 policy
keys are bracketed to keep host and port unambiguous. Whitespace and NUL are
rejected before resolution.

The first product-specific database component operation is `pg-simple-query`.
It emits the PostgreSQL `Q` frame over a verified TLS channel and accepts only
the bounded AuthenticationOk followed by ReadyForQuery response used by this
slice. This operation assumes an already-authenticated TLS endpoint or proxy;
it does not claim PostgreSQL startup or authentication negotiation.

## Maturity boundary

PostgreSQL SSLRequest, StartupMessage, SASL/SCRAM authentication, general
backend message streaming, cancellation and transaction orchestration remain
open. External PKI/revocation and real-browser bridge evidence also remain
outside this qualification."}]
